.TH WIFI 8 "October 2026" "wifi-cli 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
wifi \- scan, pick and connect to a Wi-Fi network from a headless shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wifi
.RI [ \-i\ iface ]
.br
.B wifi
.RI [ \-i\ iface ]
.I ssid password
.br
.B wifi
.RI [ \-i\ iface ]
.BR status | disable | forget
.br
.B wifi
.BR \-h | \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.B wifi
scans for networks on the first wireless interface it finds, presents a
numbered list, prompts for a passphrase, writes the supplicant configuration,
and waits until the interface is routable. The connection is persistent across
reboots.
.PP
Given an
.I ssid
and
.IR password ,
it connects without prompting. Pass
.B NONE
as the password for an open network.
.PP
On systems where NetworkManager manages the interface,
.B wifi
delegates to
.BR nmcli (1)
instead of configuring wpa_supplicant directly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show link state, address and the backend's view of the interface.
.TP
.B disable
Stop and disable the
.BI wpa_supplicant@ iface
unit. The saved network is kept.
.TP
.B forget
As
.BR disable ,
and also remove the saved network configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i\  iface ", " \-\-iface= iface
Operate on
.I iface
instead of the first wireless interface found.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant\- iface .conf
Generated network configuration (mode 0600, PSK hash only). Read by the stock
.BI wpa_supplicant@ iface
systemd unit.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/80\-wifi\-cli.network
Shipped systemd\-networkd unit matching
.BR Type=wlan ;
enables DHCP with route metric 2048 so a wired link keeps the default route.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Connected.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, missing dependency, or no wireless interface.
.TP
.B 2
Supplicant started but the interface did not become routable within 20 seconds.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive setup from a serial console:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo wifi
.RE
.PP
Unattended first boot:
.PP
.RS
.B wifi 'Site3-Mgmt' 'correct horse battery staple'
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wpa_supplicant (8),
.BR wpa_passphrase (8),
.BR networkctl (1),
.BR systemd.network (5),
.BR iw (8),
.BR nmcli (1)
